%% seq_03b_marketplace_process_application.mmd
%% Updated 2026-06-26 (verified).
%% Reader intent: Understand how an organizer decision converts a proposal into approval, rejection, and possible assignment side effects.
%% Key boundary: Decision-processing only; initial proposal submit and withdraw behavior are separate flows.
%% Current caveat: Approval can also create assignment and reject competing proposals, so one decision may fan out into multiple writes.
%% Storage caveat: Phase 1 updates task_applications. marketplace_applications is parked for a later storage migration.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Creator as Creator / Project Owner / Manager
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as ProcessMarketplaceApplicationController
    participant Cmd as ProcessMarketplaceApplicationCommand
    participant Repo as TaskRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Evt as Event Bus

    Creator->>B: Choose approve / reject
    B->>C: POST /applications/:id/process
    C->>Cmd: execute(dto)
    Cmd->>Repo: load proposal + task
    Repo->>DB: SELECT task_application, task
    DB-->>Repo: Results
    Cmd->>Cmd: validate process permission

    alt Approve
        Cmd->>Repo: update proposal approved
        Repo->>DB: UPDATE task_applications (runtime truth)
        Cmd->>Repo: create task assignment
        Repo->>DB: INSERT task_assignments
        Cmd->>Repo: update task assignee + reject others
        Repo->>DB: UPDATE tasks and other proposals
        Cmd->>Evt: emit task:application:approved
    else Reject
        Cmd->>Repo: update proposal rejected
        Repo->>DB: UPDATE task_applications (runtime truth)
        Cmd->>Evt: emit task:application:rejected
    end

    C-->>B: Redirect back
    B-->>Creator: Updated proposal status
